            <ArticleTitle>Flared sign of flail mandible on computed tomography: an unstable fracture associated with a compromised airway.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>968-970</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0266-4356(17)30638-1</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bjoms.2017.08.359</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A mandibular fracture alone rarely causes a life-threatening injury. The aim of this paper was to emphasise the importance of prompt identification of the radiological signs of a flail mandible in a patient with maxillofacial trauma who eventually needed definitive management of her airway.</AbstractText>
